---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Bulk Website Speed Test — Test Multiple Websites at Once (Free)"
  description="Free bulk website speed test: test multiple websites' speed at once with Google PageSpeed — performance scores, Core Web Vitals (LCP, CLS, TBT), and top fixes per URL. Batch test up to 10 sites, no login."
  keywords={[
    'bulk website speed test',
    'test multiple websites speed',
    'website speed test multiple urls',
    'batch pagespeed test',
    'website performance test',
    'core web vitals checker',
    'lighthouse speed test online',
    'bulk site speed checker',
  ]}
  path="/speed-test"
>
  <section class="intro">
    <h1>Bulk Website Speed Test — Test Multiple Sites at Once</h1>
    <p>
      Paste up to 10 URLs and test them all at once — performance scores, Core Web Vitals,
      and the top fixes for each, in a single batch. Built for agencies and developers
      auditing whole client portfolios, not just one page at a time.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="tool">
    <form id="st-form">
      <label class="field-label" for="st-urls">One URL per line (max 10)</label>
      <textarea
        id="st-urls"
        rows="6"
        placeholder="example.com&#10;https://another-site.org/page&#10;https://third.net"
        required
      ></textarea>
      <div class="row">
        <button type="submit" id="st-submit">Run batch test</button>
        <span id="st-status" class="status mono" role="status" aria-live="polite"></span>
      </div>
    </form>

    <div id="st-results" class="results"></div>
  </section>

  <!-- Ad slot: in-content — paste your AdSense unit here after approval -->
  <div class="ad-slot" data-ad-slot="in-content"></div>

  <section class="explainer">
    <h2>Why a <em>bulk</em> speed test?</h2>
    <p>
      Most free speed tools test one URL at a time. If you manage a dozen client sites, or
      want to compare your pages against competitors before and after a redesign, clicking
      through a single-URL tool ten times is tedious. This tool runs a batch: paste up to
      10 URLs, submit once, and get a per-URL breakdown — Google PageSpeed performance
      score, the Core Web Vitals that matter for rankings (Largest Contentful Paint,
      Cumulative Layout Shift, Total Blocking Time), and the two or three highest-impact
      fixes Lighthouse suggests for each URL.
    </p>
    <p>
      Tests run against the mobile strategy, since that's what Google uses for indexing.
      Each URL in your batch is tested independently — if one site is down or fails its
      audit, you still get results for the rest. URLs are processed through this site's
      own serverless function to Google's PageSpeed Insights API; nothing is stored.
    </p>
    <p class="mono small">https:// prepended automatically if you leave it off.</p>

    <h2>FAQ</h2>
    <div class="faq">
      <details>
        <summary>Why is the limit 10 URLs per batch?</summary>
        <p>
          Each PageSpeed audit takes several seconds of real time, and the free API tier is
          rate-limited. Ten keeps every batch fast, fair, and free for everyone. Run
          multiple batches if you have more sites.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>What do the vitals mean?</summary>
        <p>
          <strong>LCP</strong> (Largest Contentful Paint) measures loading: good is under
          2.5s. <strong>CLS</strong> (Cumulative Layout Shift) measures visual stability:
          good is under 0.1. <strong>TBT</strong> (Total Blocking Time) measures
          interactivity: good is under 200ms.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>One of my URLs failed. Why didn't the whole batch fail?</summary>
        <p>
          Every URL is tested independently and errors are reported per-row. A private,
          redirecting, or unreachable URL shows its own inline error; the rest of your
          results are unaffected.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Do you store the URLs I test?</summary>
        <p>
          No. URLs are sent to our serverless function, forwarded to Google's PageSpeed
          API for the audit, and discarded. There's no database — see the
          <a href="/privacy-policy">privacy policy</a>.
        </p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </section>

  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'FAQPage',
    mainEntity: [
      {
        '@type': 'Question',
        name: 'Why is the limit 10 URLs per batch?',
        acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: 'Each PageSpeed audit takes several seconds of real time, and the free API tier is rate-limited. Ten keeps every batch fast, fair, and free for everyone.' },
      },
      {
        '@type': 'Question',
        name: 'What do the vitals mean?',
        acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: 'LCP (Largest Contentful Paint) measures loading: good is under 2.5s. CLS (Cumulative Layout Shift) measures visual stability: good is under 0.1. TBT (Total Blocking Time) measures interactivity: good is under 200ms.' },
      },
      {
        '@type': 'Question',
        name: 'One of my URLs failed. Why didn\u2019t the whole batch fail?',
        acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: 'Every URL is tested independently and errors are reported per-row. A private, redirecting, or unreachable URL shows its own inline error; the rest of your results are unaffected.' },
      },
      {
        '@type': 'Question',
        name: 'Do you store the URLs I test?',
        acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: 'No. URLs are sent to our serverless function, forwarded to Google. PageSpeed API for the audit, and discarded. There is no database.' },
      },
    ],
  })} />

  <script>
    const form = document.getElementById('st-form') as HTMLFormElement;
    const textarea = document.getElementById('st-urls') as HTMLTextAreaElement;
    const submitBtn = document.getElementById('st-submit') as HTMLButtonElement;
    const statusEl = document.getElementById('st-status')!;
    const resultsEl = document.getElementById('st-results')!;
    const MAX_URLS = 10;

    form.addEventListener('submit', async (e) => {
      e.preventDefault();

      const urls = normalizeUrls(textarea.value);
      if (urls.length === 0) {
        statusEl.textContent = 'Enter at least one valid URL.';
        return;
      }
      if (urls.length > MAX_URLS) {
        statusEl.textContent = `Max ${MAX_URLS} URLs per batch — you entered ${urls.length}. Remove ${urls.length - MAX_URLS}.`;
        return;
      }

      submitBtn.disabled = true;
      statusEl.textContent = 'Testing… this can take up to a minute.';
      resultsEl.innerHTML = renderQueued(urls);

      try {
        const res = await fetch('/api/speed-check', {
          method: 'POST',
          headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
          body: JSON.stringify({ urls }),
        });
        if (res.status === 404) {
          statusEl.textContent =
            'The speed-test backend only runs on the deployed site (Cloudflare Pages). To test locally: add your PageSpeed API key to .dev.vars (see .dev.vars.example) and run npm run preview:pages';
          resultsEl.innerHTML = '';
          return;
        }
        if (!res.ok) {
          const detail = await res.json().catch(() => null);
          throw new Error(detail?.error || `Server returned ${res.status}`);
        }
        const results = await res.json();
        renderResults(results);
        statusEl.textContent = '';
      } catch (err) {
        statusEl.textContent = `Failed: ${(err as Error).message}`;
      } finally {
        submitBtn.disabled = false;
      }
    });

    function normalizeUrls(value: string): string[] {
      return value
        .split('\n')
        .map((line) => line.trim())
        .filter((line) => line.length > 0)
        .map((line) => (/^https?:\/\//i.test(line) ? line : `https://${line}`))
        .filter((line) => {
          try {
            const u = new URL(line);
            return !!u.hostname && !!u.hostname.includes('.');
          } catch {
            return false;
          }
        });
    }

    interface RowResult {
      url: string;
      ok: boolean;
      score?: number;
      lcp?: string;
      cls?: string;
      tbt?: string;
      opportunities?: string[];
      error?: string;
    }

    function renderQueued(urls: string[]): string {
      return urls
        .map(
          (url) => `
          <div class="result-row queued" data-url="${escapeAttr(url)}">
            <div class="url mono">${escapeHtml(url)}</div>
            <div class="row-state mono">queued → testing…</div>
          </div>`
        )
        .join('');
    }

    function renderResults(results: RowResult[]): void {
      resultsEl.innerHTML = results.map(renderRow).join('');
    }

    function renderRow(r: RowResult): string {
      const urlLine = `<div class="url mono">${escapeHtml(r.url)}</div>`;
      if (!r.ok) {
        return `<div class="result-row error">${urlLine}<div class="row-state mono">${escapeHtml(r.error || 'Test failed')}</div></div>`;
      }
      const scoreColor = r.score! >= 90 ? 'good' : r.score! >= 50 ? 'warn' : 'bad';
      const opps = (r.opportunities ?? [])
        .map((o) => `<li>${escapeHtml(o)}</li>`)
        .join('');
      return `
        <div class="result-row done">
          ${urlLine}
          <div class="metrics">
            <div class="score ${scoreColor} mono">${r.score}<span class="unit">/100</span></div>
            <div class="vitals mono">
              <span>LCP <strong>${escapeHtml(r.lcp ?? '—')}</strong></span>
              <span>CLS <strong>${escapeHtml(r.cls ?? '—')}</strong></span>
              <span>TBT <strong>${escapeHtml(r.tbt ?? '—')}</strong></span>
            </div>
          </div>
          ${opps ? `<ul class="opps">${opps}</ul>` : ''}
        </div>`;
    }

    function escapeHtml(s: string): string {
      const div = document.createElement('div');
      div.textContent = s;
      return div.innerHTML;
    }
    function escapeAttr(s: string): string {
      return escapeHtml(s).replace(/"/g, '&quot;');
    }
  </script>

  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'WebApplication',
    name: 'Bulk Website Speed Test',
    url: 'https://devtoolbench.dev/speed-test',
    applicationCategory: 'DeveloperApplication',
    operatingSystem: 'Any (web browser)',
    offers: { '@type': 'Offer', price: '0', priceCurrency: 'USD' },
    description: 'Free bulk website speed test: run Google PageSpeed audits on up to 10 URLs at once with performance scores, Core Web Vitals, and top optimization opportunities.',
  })} />

  <aside class="related">
    <h2>More free tools from DevToolbench</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="/breach-checker">Password breach checker — check if your email was hacked</a></li>
      <li><a href="/fake-data-generator">Mock data generator — fake JSON, CSV &amp; SQL test data</a></li>
    </ul>
  </aside>

  <style>
    .related { max-width: 46rem; margin: 0 0 2rem; padding: 1rem 1.25rem; background: var(--bg-raised); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 8px; }
    .related h2 { font-size: 1rem; margin: 0 0 0.5rem; }
    .related ul { margin: 0; padding-left: 1.25rem; font-size: 0.9375rem; }
    .related li { margin: 0.25rem 0; }

    .intro { padding: 2rem 0 0.5rem; }
    .intro h1 { margin: 0 0 0.5rem; font-size: 1.75rem; }
    .intro p { color: var(--text-dim); max-width: 44rem; margin: 0; }

    .tool {
      background: var(--bg-raised);
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: 10px;
      padding: 1.5rem;
      margin: 1.5rem 0;
    }
    .field-label { display: block; font-size: 0.875rem; margin-bottom: 0.375rem; color: var(--text-dim); }
    textarea {
      width: 100%;
      background: var(--bg-input);
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: 6px;
      padding: 0.75rem;
      color: var(--text);
      font-family: var(--mono);
      font-size: 0.875rem;
      resize: vertical;
    }
    .row { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 1rem; margin-top: 0.75rem; flex-wrap: wrap; }
    .row button {
      background: var(--good);
      color: #04211d;
      border: none;
      border-radius: 6px;
      padding: 0.625rem 1.25rem;
      font-weight: 600;
      cursor: pointer;
    }
    .row button:hover { filter: brightness(1.1); }
    .row button:disabled { opacity: 0.6; cursor: wait; }
    .status { font-size: 0.8125rem; color: var(--text-dim); }

    .results { margin-top: 1.25rem; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.75rem; }
    .result-row {
      background: var(--bg-input);
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: 8px;
      padding: 0.875rem 1rem;
    }
    .result-row.queued .row-state { color: var(--text-dim); animation: pulse 1.5s ease-in-out infinite; }
    @keyframes pulse { 50% { opacity: 0.4; } }
    .result-row.error { border-color: var(--bad); }
    .result-row.error .row-state { color: var(--bad); }
    .url { font-size: 0.8125rem; word-break: break-all; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; color: var(--text); }
    .metrics { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 1.25rem; flex-wrap: wrap; }
    .score { font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 700; }
    .score .unit { font-size: 0.75rem; font-weight: 400; color: var(--text-dim); }
    .score.good { color: var(--good); }
    .score.warn { color: var(--warn); }
    .score.bad { color: var(--bad); }
    .vitals { display: flex; gap: 1rem; flex-wrap: wrap; font-size: 0.8125rem; color: var(--text-dim); }
    .vitals strong { color: var(--text); }
    .opps { margin: 0.75rem 0 0; padding-left: 1.25rem; color: var(--text-dim); font-size: 0.875rem; }

    .explainer { max-width: 46rem; padding: 1rem 0 2rem; }
    .explainer h2 { font-size: 1.25rem; margin-top: 2rem; }
    .explainer p { color: var(--text-dim); font-size: 0.9375rem; }
    .explainer .small { font-size: 0.8125rem; }
    .faq details {
      background: var(--bg-raised);
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: 8px;
      padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
      margin-top: 0.5rem;
    }
    .faq summary { font-weight: 600; }
    .faq summary::marker { color: var(--good); }
    .faq p { color: var(--text-dim); font-size: 0.9375rem; }
  </style>
</Layout>
